    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "feature/wounds-tending-in-the-crate",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(native): tend the wounded as one crate pass\n\nFormationWounds.tend is now one call, `wounds_step` (`wounds/pass.rs`,\nspec 39 step 8b5-xxiv): the listed squads' living units and bodies\nlying are read in the crate, the takings run, and each body taken lands\nthere - captured (TAKEN), sent home (the leader's messenger spent,\nRELEASED, the body's side standing shocked) or finished (DEAD) - with\n\"captured\", \"sent_home\" and \"finished\" (new in events::KINDS) in the\nlog. GDScript mirrors the states and the messengers, then takes the\nlog. The `wounds_tend` binding and its decoder are removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi3y5NTE4DKmXnwc68q",
    "head_sha": "571a3c45f4b82c5edd26a161077c4aefa778a612",
